CaCertificates                                  RISC OS on Linux
==============
Mozilla's bundle of root certificates (as curl.se and Python's certifi
publish it), so that programs which check secure (https) connections
with curl or OpenSSL - PackMan among them - can. It sets
CaCertificates$Dir when the machine starts; the bundle is
<CaCertificates$Dir>.ca-certificates/crt.

The certificate data is Mozilla's, under the Mozilla Public Licence 2.0
(https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/).
